                        LOAD-BEARING GOTCHAS rediscovered, also relevant to
                        Phase 6/7 (any future set_channel-shaped write):

                        (i) PORT BOUNCE FOR set_channel. The Meshtastic firmware
                        buffers channel-slot changes in RAM and only commits to
                        flash when the serial session ends (DTR drop). pip-mesh
                        gets this for free because it uses `echo > $tty` (a
                        fresh open/close per write); our long-lived fd has to
                        close+reopen explicitly or the write LOOKS accepted
                        (verify-cycle handshake succeeds) but is silently
                        dropped on the next device read or reboot, and pip-mesh
                        later sees no change. set_owner and set_lora_config are
                        stored differently and do NOT need the bounce. Added
                        pn_mesh_serial_reopen() and the connection now bounces
                        the fd between the set_channel write and the verify
                        cycle. Phase 6's QR-import path will write multiple
                        channels in sequence -- bundle them in a single
                        begin_edit_settings(64)/commit_edit_settings(65)
                        transaction (per pip-mesh's --copy-channels) and one
                        bounce at the end.

                        (ii) use-after-free across the modal-destroy in the Add
                        dialog: gtk_entry_get_text returns a pointer INTO the
                        entry's buffer; destroying the dialog frees the entry.
                        The async write's internal g_strdup runs AFTER the
                        destroy, picking up freed memory -- the channel name
                        comes back as garbage on the next read-back. Fix:
                        g_strdup the entry text BEFORE destroying the dialog.
                        (psk_bytes was already safe because decode_psk_hex
                        mallocs a fresh buffer we own.)

                        (iii) UX: a 3-5s verify cycle with no visible motion
                        reads as "the app froze". Add a GtkSpinner next to the
                        action button, spin while writing=TRUE. Identity (Apply
                        owner) and Region (Apply LoRa) have the same delay and
                        would benefit from the same spinner -- not added yet
                        (user didn't ask), one-liner each when wanted.
           [x] Known Known Nodes page (out-of-band insertion between Nodes Phase
               5 and Phase 6 -- user-requested "everything works" diagnostic).
               Read-only sortable GtkTreeView over PnMeshState->nodes; the
               device's own row is bolded and pinned to the top via a hidden
               is_us primary sort key, with columns ID / Short / Long / HW /
               Role / Hops / SNR / Last heard / Battery. Last heard / SNR /
               Battery use separate numeric sort columns so the displayed
               strings ("3m ago", "—") sort by value not ASCII. Connection now
               captures the full NodeInfo set (added field defines NI_SNR=4,
               NI_LAST_HEARD=5, NI_DEVICE_METRICS=6, NI_HOPS_AWAY=9, U_ROLE=7;
               new parse_device_metrics; SeenNode extended with
               role/snr/last_heard/hops_away/battery/voltage) and publishes
               PnMeshState->nodes (GPtrArray of new public type PnMeshNode).
               format_hw_model / format_role lifted out of page-identity into
                        libpipnode-core (lib/pn-mesh-formats.{c,h}) so
                        the new page reuses the same tables. Files
                        shipped: lib/pn-mesh-formats.{c,h} (core);
                        lib/pn-mesh-page-known-nodes.{c,h} (gui).  No new
                        unit test -- the page is a pure render layer over
                        already-tested protobuf parsing; the existing
                        test-pn-mesh-pb / test-pn-mesh-frame net still holds. No
                        protocol writes; no admin frames; no ABI bump
                        (PnMeshState is internal to the dialog). Phase numbering
                        unchanged below; "Phase 5.5" would misread, so it's
                        tracked here as an inline entry.

           [x] Phase 6 Share page (headline feature). Single-QR page living
                        under the Radio tab as a third expander (Region & LoRa /
                        Channels / Share). Top: subtitle line that rephrases per
                        mode. Channel checkbox list (primary pre-checked; rows
                        are the device's non-disabled slots). Mode-toggle radio
                        group ("Share channels (additive)" vs "Share full config
                        (replaces)") -- exactly one QR drawn from the active
                        mode so a phone camera cannot lock on the wrong code.
                        Below the radios: a single cairo-rendered QR (when
                        libqrencode is present at build time, else a "install
                        libqrencode and rebuild" notice). Underneath the QR: a
                        wrapping selectable monospace GtkLabel showing the full
                        URL + a clipboard Copy button (Label not GtkEntry -- a
                        single-line entry hides the dynamic tail behind
                        the identical "https://meshtastic.org/e/#" prefix
                        and the user cannot tell when the URL changed). URL
                        builder lives in libpipnode-core (pn-mesh-qr
                        .{c,h}) as a pure-C, GTK-free port of pip-mesh's
                        build_channel_set_hex + print_qr_url; cairo render (and
                        the libqrencode include) lives in the gui-side
                        page-share.c so the core tier stays headless.

                        ChannelSet wire layout (pip-mesh-compatible):
                          ChannelSet {
                            repeated ChannelSettings settings = 1; // embedded
                            LoRaConfig               lora     = 2; // optional
                          }
                          ChannelSettings { bytes psk = 2; string name = 3; }
                          LoRaConfig (QR subset):
                            bool use_preset = 1; ModemPreset modem = 2;
                            RegionCode region = 7; uint32 hop_limit = 8;
                        URL = "https://meshtastic.org/e/#" + base64url
                        (RFC 4648 with '+'->'-', '/'->'_', trailing '='
                        stripped) of the serialized ChannelSet.

                        Optional dep: libqrencode (PKG_CHECK_MODULES, AC_DEFINE
                        HAVE_QRENCODE, AM_CONDITIONAL); auto-detected, URL-only
                        fallback paints a "install libqrencode and rebuild"
                        notice in the QR slot when missing. Configure prints
                        "libqrencode not found; Meshtastic Share page will show
                        URLs only" in that case.

                        Files shipped: lib/pn-mesh-qr.{c,h} (core),
                        lib/pn-mesh-page-share.{c,h} (gui); deltas in
                        lib/pn-mesh-dialog.c (third expander on Radio tab,
                        set_state on connect/drop, GtkOverlay loading spinner
                        over the notebook -- see UX FOLLOW-UPS below) and
                        lib/Makefile.am (QRENCODE_CFLAGS/LIBS on the gui lib).
                        Unit test tests/unit/ test-pn-mesh-qr.c (5 cases, 19
                        checks) pins byte-for-byte URL match for a single
                        default channel and for the full-config form, plus
                        skip-disabled, selection-subset and empty-error paths.

                        UX FOLLOW-UPS landed with Phase 6:

                        - Handshake loading overlay. The 3-5s handshake would
                        otherwise let the user switch to a tab whose state
                        hasn't arrived and read it as "device has no channels /
                        no MQTT". Notebook is now wrapped in a GtkOverlay with a
                        64x64 centred GtkSpinner + "Reading configuration from
                        device…" label; show_loading/hide_loading also flip
                        notebook sensitivity so tabs cannot be clicked while the
                        spinner is up. drop_connection hides it too so a
                        dialog-close mid-handshake leaves no ghost widget.

                        - Channels page list height. set_min_content_height(220)
                        + set_propagate_natural_height(TRUE) + a hard
                        set_size_request(list, -1, 200) on the GtkListBox
                        itself. Without all three, the FALSE/ FALSE-packed
                        Channels expander pinned the scrolled list to a single
                        row. Same pattern (with smaller numbers) used for the
                        Share page's channel checkbox list -- the QR area's
                        set_size_request was eating the slack the list needed.

                        - Trash-can delete glyph. Per-row delete on the Channels
                        page uses "user-trash-symbolic" (verified present in the
                        icon theme) instead of "edit-delete"; reads as "discard"
                        rather than "erase".

                        GOTCHAS for future cousins (Phase 7 / 11+):

                        (i) ProtoBuf field numbers in pip-mesh's bash docstrings
                        were not always accurate (Phase 5 already hit this on
                        set_channel: docstring 32, code 33). For Phase 6 the
                        field numbers came verbatim out of build_channel_set_hex
                        / print_qr_config and matched what the firmware expects;
                        the test pins them at the URL level so a future "tidy
                        up" cannot silently drift.

                        (ii) Region UNSET would brick the receiver on
                        full-config import (proto3 zero == UNSET, no fall-back).
                        refresh_url skips emission in full-config mode unless
                        PnMeshState->have_lora_config is TRUE (a small dim
                        notice paints in its place) so the URL/QR pair stays
                        blank (not "garbage URL") until the handshake actually
                        surfaces a LoRa config.

                        (iii) Cairo QR render budgets four modules of quiet zone
                        around the matrix even though Meshtastic phone apps are
                        tolerant; without it the white border collapses when the
                        dialog uses a dark theme and decode rate drops. Drawing
                        happens against the cached URL so toggle->draw is one
                        cycle of queue_draw -- no re-encode on every expose.

                        (iv) GtkScrolledWindow's set_min_content_height ALONE
                        was repeatedly observed to be ignored when the scrolled
                        window lives inside a GtkExpander packed FALSE/FALSE in
                        a tab box: the listbox collapsed to one row. The
                        reliable recipe is min_content_height +
                        propagate_natural_height + an explicit
                        gtk_widget_set_size_request on the listbox itself. Any
                        future tab-hosted scrolled list (Phase 7 test page,
                        Phase 11+ module pages) should follow the same
                        belt-and-braces pattern.

                        (v) Long URLs in a single-line GtkEntry hide their
                        dynamic suffix behind the (identical) URL prefix.
                        Wrapping selectable GtkLabel was the right widget; reuse
                        it for any other "show me this URL" affordance instead
                        of an entry.
           [x] Phase 7 Test page. Channel picker + message entry + Send; below,
                        a live "Incoming traffic" log running monitor on the
                        open connection. Auto-stops on dialog close. Shipped as
                        the Diagnostics tab's "Test" expander alongside Known
                        Nodes; PORTNUM_TEXT_MESSAGE_APP =1 wire defines on the
                        ToRadio side, MeshPacket parser on the FromRadio side
                        queues PnMeshTextEvent records the dialog drains via a
                        200 ms timer (pump_monitor + take_text_event).
                        Synthesised "outgoing" events are echoed back from
                        send_text_sync so a single transcript shows both
                        directions. Per dialog-lifetime rule the monitor timer
                        is owned by MeshDialogCtx (start in on_connection_ready,
                        stop in drop_connection / dialog dispose), and
                        pump_monitor is skipped while any write is in flight via
                        the busy_count so the frame reader does not race the
                        worker thread.
