[ ] 33 Meshtastic discovery: stop treating a BARE 10c4:ea60 as a Meshtastic
       device. The VID:PID table in lib/pn-mesh-discover.c (KNOWN_DEVICES)
       matches the Heltec V3 on 10c4:ea60 -- but that is the GENERIC Silicon
       Labs CP2102 /
       CP2102N USB-UART chip, used by countless unrelated boards. In particular
       the common Sonoff/ITead Zigbee dongles (ZBDongle-P) are CP2102N ->
       10c4:ea60, so a plugged-in Zigbee coordinator shows up in the Meshtastic
       dialog as a "Heltec V3". Picking it aims the Meshtastic want_config_id
       handshake at a Z-Stack UART (root cause of the 2026-05-29 zigbee2mqtt
       CPU-spin incident: pipnode opened the shared /dev/ttyUSB and wrote
       Meshtastic frames into it; zigbee2mqtt choked on the corrupted byte
       stream).

         MITIGATED 2026-05-29 (see the in-use guard added the same day): such a
         device, while it is open by zigbee2mqtt (or anything else), now appears
         DISABLED in the list with an "in use by <proc>" note and can never be
         opened (pn_mesh_tty_in_use + TIOCEXCL in pn-mesh-serial.c). But that
         only helps WHILE the other process holds the port -- an idle, unclaimed
         CP2102 Zigbee dongle would still be mislabelled "Heltec V3" and be
         connectable.

         THE WORK (why it is hard): sysfs alone cannot disambiguate -- the
         product / manufacturer / serial strings are the chip's generic defaults
         ("CP2102 USB to UART Bridge Controller" / "Silicon Labs"), identical on
         a Heltec and a Zigbee dongle. The only reliable tell is a safe,
         read-only probe over the wire (e.g. a Meshtastic want_config_id and a
         bounded wait for a valid 0x94 0xC3 frame) -- but ANY write is exactly
         what we must NOT do to a non-Meshtastic device. Options to weigh: (a)
         mark generic-CP2102 matches as "unverified / possibly another device"
         in the UI and require an explicit user confirm before the first write;
         (b) keep a denylist of known-NON-mesh CP2102 product/serial strings;
         (c) cross-check against a system Zigbee/serial registry. None is clean;
         deferred deliberately.

[ ] 36 Stop ModemManager from probing Meshtastic serial devices. When a tty
       appears, ModemManager (root) opens it and fires AT commands -- which
       toggles DTR/RTS (rebooting the ESP32) and races pipnode's open. pipnode's
       in-use guard is a /proc scan that can't see root-owned holders, so it
       misses MM. Fix: ship a udev rule setting ID_MM_DEVICE_IGNORE=1 for the
       Meshtastic VID:PIDs (packaging step), and/or inhibit the device over MM's
       D-Bus API around open. Caveat: 10c4:ea60 is generic CP2102 (see #33); a
       blanket ignore also hides real CP2102 modems. Touches system config --
       weigh against the minimal-invasive-packaging line.

[ ] 39 Node source code-review findings (from the 2026-06-01 fan-out review of
       every node-implementing source file -- ~70 core lib/pn-*.c nodes + 30
       -gui.c companions, the network/ollama/tasmota/sound-effects plugins, and
       the 54 plugins/image/pn-image-*.c filters). Overall the tree is in very
       good shape: timer/idle/thread teardown in dispose/finalize, GObject
       refcounting + g_free pairing, the value>0.5 boolean convention, FA-4.7
       icons, and the shared rowstride-aware plugins/image/pn-image-ops.c helper
       layer are all sound. These are the individual issues worth fixing, each
       tracked separately below. (The hand-rolled WARNING_ICON nodes the review
       also re-flagged -- pn-inject, pn-sound, pn-tts, ollama, sci-fi-sound,
       tasmota/* -- are already TODO #31.3. The subprocess-spawn items M6/M7/L4
       are the same "pure C, no helper subprocess" theme as #38.1, which covers
       PnHttp/curl specifically.)

         HIGH
         [x] 39.1 Ollama silently drops every message when "hostname" is empty
               (plugins/ollama/pn-ollama.c:370). Empty hostname is the INTENDED
               default -- build_endpoint resolves ""->localhost and
               refresh_visual_state shows the node as configured with only a
               model set -- but receive()'s guard also rejects empty hostname,
               so a freshly dropped Ollama node looks green/ready yet swallows
               all input. Fix: drop the hostname clause from the receive() guard
               to match refresh_visual_state / build_endpoint.

         MEDIUM
         [ ] 39.2 Expression parser has no recursion-depth limit ->
               C-stack-overflow crash on pathological nesting
               (lib/pn-expr-parser.c, the parse_factor<->parse_expression
               recursive descent). A configured expression like ((((...)))) or a
               long unary-minus chain overflows the native stack and crashes the
               process with no recovery. Input is local node config (not
               network-facing), so impact is a user pasting a bad expression.
               Fix: add a depth counter to Ctx and error out past a sane limit.
               (pn-var-store.c's evaluator recurses to the same depth; the
               parser is the gate that builds the tree.)
         [ ] 39.3 Graph 3D line mode overflows the PLplot cmap0 with >=9 series
               (lib/pn-graph-gui.c:922). paint_line_3d writes each series colour
               to cmap0 slot 8+i (up to 19 for the 12-series cap) but
               paint_setup_page never grows the colormap (no plscmap0n) and the
               default cmap0 holds only 16 entries (0-15); series past slot 15
               render in a stale/wrong colour. Fix: plscmap0n(8 + nseries)
               before the per-series loop in the 3D paths. (3D-histogram path is
               unaffected -- it reuses low slots.) Triggers only at 9+ topics.
         [x] 39.4 Table cell/title truncation can emit invalid UTF-8
               (lib/pn-table-gui.c:80, fit_text_with_ellipsis). The first
               truncation pass cuts at a fixed 252-byte offset that is not
               codepoint-aligned, so the inserted ellipsis can follow a partial
               code point; the step-back realign loop only runs on SUBSEQUENT
               passes, never the initial cut. cairo renders tofu. Fix: align the
               first cut to a UTF-8 boundary (g_utf8_find_prev_char). Triggers
               only on >252-byte strings.
         [ ] 39.5 Image Pixelate dereferences dst before its NULL check
               (plugins/image/pn-image-pixelate.c:54,56).
               gdk_pixbuf_get_rowstride /_get_pixels are called on dst before
               the `if (dst == NULL) return` guard at :59, so the guard is dead
               and a failed gdk_pixbuf_copy crashes the GTask worker thread.
               Fix: move the NULL check above the dereferences. Low probability
               (copy only fails on OOM) but a clear regression against the
               pattern every sibling node follows.
         [x] 39.6 Image Dither has no NULL check on dst at all
               (plugins/image/pn-image-dither.c:62-64) -- dst =
               gdk_pixbuf_copy(src) is immediately dereferenced (unlike every
               sibling). NULL dst -> crash; the buf malloc at :51 also leaks on
               that (currently impossible) path. Fix: add the standard NULL
               guard + free buf.
               DONE 2026-06-01: dither_transform now checks dst == NULL right
               after gdk_pixbuf_copy and, if so, g_free(buf) + return NULL
               before the rowstride/pixels dereferences -- matching the sibling
               guard in pn-image-pixelate.c.
         [ ] 39.7 Sound node spawns `paplay PATH` (lib/pn-sound.c:151-188),
               violating the "pure C, no helper subprocesses at runtime" rule.
               Implement audio playback in-process. (on_play_done itself is safe
               -- holds a ref on self, main-thread-only state.) Sibling theme to
               #38.1.
         [ ] 39.8 Text-to-Speech shells out extensively (lib/pn-tts.c): `sh -c
               <cmd>` per utterance (:433-475, :1040-1095, :1171-1288),
               g_spawn_command_line_sync for `pactl list sinks`, and `<engine>
               --voices` enumeration -- the most subprocess use in the tree.
               Port to in-process C. Sibling theme to #38.1.

         LOW / NIT
         [ ] 39.9 Numeric readout can cast an out-of-range double to gint64 (UB)
               before the overload check (lib/pn-numeric-gui.c:199-201). With
               digits=12/decimals=6, scale=1e6; a finite but huge data.value
               (e.g. 1e300) makes av*scale ~1e306 and `(gint64)
               floor(av*scale+0.5)` is computed BEFORE the `int_part > max_int`
               guard. read_value only filters non-finite, not
               out-of-gint64-range. Fix: clamp av (or test av*scale against
               G_MAXINT64) before the cast.
         [ ] 39.10 Rewrite/Filter report bad-JSON-after-expansion via g_warning
               (lib/pn-rewrite.c:225, lib/pn-filter.c:143), invisible under the
               desktop launcher; convention prefers a node failure message /
               log.
         [ ] 39.11 Ollama cancellation lives in finalize, not dispose
               (plugins/ollama/pn-ollama.c:536-543), so it never aborts an
               in-flight request -- on_generate_done holds a strong ref on self,
               so finalize cannot run until the request completes and the
               g_cancellable_cancel is dead code for that case. No UAF, but
               closing the worksheet pins the node until Ollama replies. Fix:
               cancel in dispose (the pn-ws.c / https-tunnel pattern).
         [ ] 39.12 Sci-Fi Sound has no dispose: the g_subprocess_wait_async
               callback g_object_ref's self but the spawned media player is
               never terminated and the wait is never cancelled
               (plugins/sound-effects/pn-sci-fi-sound.c:154 + overall). No UAF
               (the ref pins self until the player exits; on_play_done is
               main-thread), but a node mid-playback can't be torn down and
               closing the worksheet leaves the player running. Also the
               per-message subprocess spawn is the #38.1 convention theme
               (likely an inherent exception for a GTK-free core audio node).
         [ ] 39.13 Ollama can pass NULL to json_node_get_object
               (plugins/ollama/pn-ollama.c:200): json-glib parses an empty/
               whitespace body as success with a NULL root, so
               json_node_get_object(json_parser_get_root(parser)) emits a
               g_critical (noisy, invisible under the launcher) before the
               subsequent `root == NULL` check handles it cleanly. Fix: NULL /
               JSON_NODE_HOLDS_OBJECT guard the root before the call.
         [ ] 39.14 TTS queue can stall on a failed re-spawn
               (lib/pn-tts.c:336-350): in on_speak_done, if pn_tts_speak fails
               to spawn the next utterance, self->speaking stays FALSE and
               on_speak_done never fires again, so the remaining backlog is
               stranded until the next inbound message (self-heals on the next
               receive). Fix: drain-retry the rest of the queue on a failed
               re-spawn.
         [ ] 39.15 HTTPS-tunnel sender wires on_accept_certificate with
               g_signal_connect (not _object) and never disconnects
               (plugins/network/pn-https-tunnel-sender.c:352). Not a live UAF --
               the handler is a pure `return TRUE` that ignores user_data and
               dies when msg is unref'd -- but fragile if it ever starts
               touching self. Fix: g_signal_connect_object or disconnect
               explicitly.

         CONSIDERED, NO ACTION (reviewed and judged not bugs; recorded so a
         future pass doesn't re-litigate them):
         - Weather-report's 15s clock_source is removed in finalize rather than
           dispose (lib/pn-weather-report.c:614) -- safe: the timeout holds no
           ref on self and only calls pn_node_request_repaint, finalize is
           reachable.
         - Meshtastic's cross-thread set_*_on_main closures g_object_ref(self)
           and briefly resurrect the object during dispose's worker join --
           legal, intentional GLib behaviour.
         - Stats' g_get_monotonic_time()-derived slot modulo
           (lib/pn-stats.c:191) -- monotonic time is non-negative on supported
           platforms.
         - 52 of the 54 image filters are clean: the shared pn-image-ops.c
           helpers (map_point/convolve/gradient/separable/median/compose) are
           rowstride-aware, (gsize)-cast against w*h*nch overflow,
           divisor==0-guarded, clamped, and NULL-checked. Only the two
           hand-rolled loops (M4, M5) slipped.

